  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656478",
      "title": "TD: Set Default Values with ngModel Property Binding",
      "lectureOrder": 519,
      "videoOrder": 475,
      "sourceHash": "98ca8cab012f4edab0a7c72f2f347e55a83f1dd5dd26a0f5502db962766345f5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "-: Thus far, we've learned a lot about the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 7.586,
          "en": "driven approach and now we can create great forms with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.586,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "Now let's move on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 12.06,
          "en": "Let's leave the world of validating user input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.06,
          "end": 16.335,
          "en": "And let's say we want to define some default values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.335,
          "end": 18.24,
          "en": "which should be displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.24,
          "end": 20.82,
          "en": "For example on the dropdown here right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.82,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "it's empty by default. Well, it would be nice if one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 26.31,
          "en": "of the two questions would be selected, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.31,
          "end": 30.81,
          "en": "For this we can change the way we add ngModel right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.81,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "We add it like this without property or event binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "No two-way data binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 40.02,
          "en": "Well, we can use it together with property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.02,
          "end": 44.1,
          "en": "So let's add some square brackets around it, no parenthesis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "So we're not using two-way binding as of now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "And now we can bind it to a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "And remember with it, I mean the control, this input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 56.82,
          "en": "which is turned into a controlled by angler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.82,
          "end": 58.62,
          "en": "in the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.62,
          "end": 63.45,
          "en": "So this selector can now be bound to a default value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.45,
          "end": 66.45,
          "en": "And you could either hard code a string into there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.45,
          "end": 68.932,
          "en": "don't forget the single quotation marks in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.932,
          "end": 73.932,
          "en": "Or you set up a property like let's say, default question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.219,
          "end": 77.46000000000001,
          "en": "which would be Pet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.46000000000001,
          "end": 80.28,
          "en": "Pet because that is one of the two valid values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.28,
          "end": 83.788,
          "en": "The other one being teacher for this question here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.788,
          "end": 86.773,
          "en": "So now we can bind this to default question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.773,
          "end": 89.894,
          "en": "And if we now save this and let it reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.894,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "you see that now Pet is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 96.63,
          "en": "And of course if we switch this to Teacher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 98.4,
          "en": "well it shouldn't be a surprise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.4,
          "end": 101.03999999999999,
          "en": "that the other value is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.03999999999999,
          "end": 103.61,
          "en": "So now all of a sudden we're using a default value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.61,
          "end": 107.16,
          "en": "And of course this does not only work for the dropdown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.16,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "it would also work for the username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 111.087,
          "en": "You could point to a default string there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.087,
          "end": 115.22999999999999,
          "en": "pre-populating this field with a default username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 117.84,
          "en": "Very useful and something you should definitely keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 119.682,
          "en": "in mind that you are not limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.682,
          "end": 122.513,
          "en": "to using ngModel without any bindings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.513,
          "end": 125.832,
          "en": "You can use one way binding, property binding to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.832,
          "end": 127.435,
          "en": "set a default value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.435,
          "end": 130.29,
          "en": "Of course, this value can still be overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 133.173,
          "en": "You can still pick a different option here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
